#: ../../source/queue-microtask_README.md:34
msgid "What is `queueMicrotask` and why would one use it?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/queue-microtask_README.md:36
msgid ""
"The `queueMicrotask` function is a WHATWG standard. It queues a microtask"
" to be executed prior to control returning to the event loop."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/queue-microtask_README.md:38
msgid ""
"A microtask is a short function which will run after the current task has"
" completed its work and when there is no other code waiting to be run "
"before control of the execution context is returned to the event loop."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/queue-microtask_README.md:40
msgid ""
"The code `queueMicrotask(fn)` is equivalent to the code "
"`Promise.resolve().then(fn)`. It is also very similar to "
"[`process.nextTick(fn)`](https://nodejs.org/api/process.html#process_process_nexttick_callback_args)"
" in Node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/queue-microtask_README.md:42
msgid ""
"Using microtasks lets code run without interfering with any other, "
"potentially higher priority, code that is pending, but before the JS "
"engine regains control over the execution context."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/queue-microtask_README.md:44
msgid ""
"See the [spec](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/timers-and-user-"
"prompts.html#microtask-queuing) or [Node "
"documentation](https://nodejs.org/api/globals.html#globals_queuemicrotask_callback)"
" for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/queue-microtask_README.md:46
msgid "Who is this package for?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/queue-microtask_README.md:48
msgid ""
"This package allows you to use `queueMicrotask` safely in all modern JS "
"engines. Use it if you prioritize small JS bundle size over support for "
"old browsers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/queue-microtask_README.md:50
msgid ""
"If you just need to support Node 12 and later, use `queueMicrotask` "
"directly. If you need to support all versions of Node, use this package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/queue-microtask_README.md:52
msgid "Why not use `process.nextTick`?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/queue-microtask_README.md:54
msgid ""
"In Node, `queueMicrotask` and `process.nextTick` are [essentially "
"equivalent](https://nodejs.org/api/globals.html#globals_queuemicrotask_callback),"
" though there are [subtle "
"differences](https://github.com/YuzuJS/setImmediate#macrotasks-and-"
"microtasks) that don't matter in most situations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/queue-microtask_README.md:56
msgid ""
"You can think of `queueMicrotask` as a standardized version of "
"`process.nextTick` that works in the browser. No need to rely on your "
"browser bundler to shim `process` for the browser environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/queue-microtask_README.md:58
msgid "Why not use `setTimeout(fn, 0)`?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/queue-microtask_README.md:60
msgid ""
"This approach is the most compatible, but it has problems. Modern "
"browsers throttle timers severely, so `setTimeout(…, 0)` usually takes at"
" least 4ms to run. Furthermore, the throttling gets even worse if the "
"page is backgrounded. If you have many `setTimeout` calls, then this can "
"severely limit the performance of your program."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/queue-microtask_README.md:62
msgid ""
"Why not use a microtask library like "
"[`immediate`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/immediate) or "
"[`asap`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/asap)?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/queue-microtask_README.md:64
msgid ""
"These packages are great! However, if you prioritize small JS bundle size"
" over optimal performance in old browsers then you may want to consider "
"this package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/queue-microtask_README.md:66
msgid ""
"This package (`queue-microtask`) is four times smaller than `immediate`, "
"twice as small as `asap`, and twice as small as using `process.nextTick` "
"and letting the browser bundler shim it automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/queue-microtask_README.md:68
msgid ""
"Note: This package throws an exception in JS environments which lack "
"`Promise` support -- which are usually very old browsers and Node.js "
"versions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/queue-microtask_README.md:70
msgid ""
"Since the `queueMicrotask` API is supported in Node.js, Chrome, Firefox, "
"Safari, Opera, and Edge, **the vast majority of users will get optimal "
"performance**. Any JS environment with `Promise`, which is almost all of "
"them, also get optimal performance. If you need support for JS "
"environments which lack `Promise` support, use one of the alternative "
"packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/queue-microtask_README.md:72
msgid "What is a shim?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/queue-microtask_README.md:74
msgid ""
"In computer programming, a shim is a library that transparently "
"intercepts API calls and changes the arguments passed, handles the "
"operation itself or redirects the operation elsewhere. – "
"[Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shim_(computing))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/queue-microtask_README.md:76
msgid "This package could also be described as a \"ponyfill\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/queue-microtask_README.md:78
msgid ""
"A ponyfill is almost the same as a polyfill, but not quite. Instead of "
"patching functionality for older browsers, a ponyfill provides that "
"functionality as a standalone module you can use. – "
"[PonyFoo](https://ponyfoo.com/articles/polyfills-or-ponyfills)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/queue-microtask_README.md:80
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/queue-microtask_README.md:82
msgid "`queueMicrotask(fn)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/queue-microtask_README.md:84
msgid "The `queueMicrotask()` method queues a microtask."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/queue-microtask_README.md:86
msgid ""
"The `fn` argument is a function to be executed after all pending tasks "
"have completed but before yielding control to the browser's event loop."
msgstr ""

